        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We believe that the five circuits are correct."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent (Lynne S. Coffin)",
      "case_id": "2002-01-1862",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5f6c3f298dad478fe059e3c9c75218f53c9aa94a7c0b0160f06491447f0b4504",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5f6c3f298dad-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 15,
        "start": 15
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The issue is not whether this harms Mr. Garceau, but whether it is appropriate under this Court's precedent to rule the way the State asked this Court to rule."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2002-01-1862",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5f6c3f298dad478fe059e3c9c75218f53c9aa94a7c0b0160f06491447f0b4504",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5f6c3f298dad-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Right."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Coffin",
      "case_id": "2002-01-1862",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5f6c3f298dad478fe059e3c9c75218f53c9aa94a7c0b0160f06491447f0b4504",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5f6c3f298dad-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. COFFIN: But Congress chose to determine that not everyone would be immediately affected -- immediately affected by AEDPA, and they --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2002-01-1862",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5f6c3f298dad478fe059e3c9c75218f53c9aa94a7c0b0160f06491447f0b4504",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5f6c3f298dad-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: How?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Coffin",
      "case_id": "2002-01-1862",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5f6c3f298dad478fe059e3c9c75218f53c9aa94a7c0b0160f06491447f0b4504",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5f6c3f298dad-0001-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. COFFIN: No. What -- what happened is there was an application for counsel. Counsel was appointed. Counsel then -- there was a stay before counsel was appointed so that counsel could be found. Then counsel was appointed, and an additional 120-day stay went into effect before counsel filed the document I'm now talking about. And this document is the Specification of Non- frivolous Issues, which includes two claims that were -- and were in the petition ultimately that put -- set forth the factual and legal basis for those two claims."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Coffin",
      "case_id": "2002-01-1862",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5f6c3f298dad478fe059e3c9c75218f53c9aa94a7c0b0160f06491447f0b4504",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5f6c3f298dad-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. COFFIN: No. What -- what I'm suggesting is that AEDPA should not be applied to Garceau either because of the first argument that I made about McFarland, or if this Court is not satisfied that, in fact, Garceau had a case pending, which is the language from Lindh that determines whether or not AEDPA should be retroactive."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Coffin",
      "case_id": "2002-01-1862",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5f6c3f298dad478fe059e3c9c75218f53c9aa94a7c0b0160f06491447f0b4504",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5f6c3f298dad-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, actually, Your Honor, since I have clients in many different positions here, I actually don't believe that it would be a problem for other capital defendants, and I do believe that it's the correct result on either basis that I have put forth for Garceau."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2002-01-1862",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5f6c3f298dad478fe059e3c9c75218f53c9aa94a7c0b0160f06491447f0b4504",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5f6c3f298dad-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Because even under AEDPA, if you just come in at the threshold, the court -- the Federal court, in general, is quite liberal about letting you develop the facts necessary to present your claim."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. McLean",
      "case_id": "2002-01-1862",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5f6c3f298dad478fe059e3c9c75218f53c9aa94a7c0b0160f06491447f0b4504",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5f6c3f298dad-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Your Honor, I respectfully disagree with that. There's nothing in AEDPA that applies whatsoever to the pre-application period. The deferential provisions of 2254(d) can only apply once an application is filed by its express terms."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
